/**

\page page_third-party_OpenBLAS LIBXSMM

\tableofcontents



[LIBXSMM](https://github.com/libxsmm/libxsmm) is a library for small, dense and
sparse matrix-matrix multiplications. Peano can use it to generate specialised,
just-in-time-compiled kernels for the small linear algebra operations that arise
in its compute kernels.

LIBXSMM is an optional dependency: it is disabled by default and Peano builds and
runs without it.


# Enable LIBXSMM

LIBXSMM is controlled through the CMake option `PEANO_WITH_LIBXSMM` (see also
\ref page_installation_home). Pass it as a `-D` flag when you configure your build
directory:

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
mkdir build && cd build
cmake .. -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DPEANO_WITH_LIBXSMM=ON
make -j
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Alternatively, toggle `PEANO_WITH_LIBXSMM` interactively through `ccmake ..`.

When the option is enabled, CMake locates LIBXSMM via `cmake/FindLIBXSMM.cmake`.
The module first searches your environment (honouring the `LIBXSMM_DIR`
environment variable and `pkg-config`); if no suitable installation is found it
fetches and builds LIBXSMM from source automatically using CMake's `FetchContent`,
so no manual installation is required.

*/
